+# Native wrapper04 private candidate (implementation snapshot06)
+
+This successor preserves native05 environment/lifecycle/ownership/resource behavior.
+The only plan change is plan04 float registration -> plan05 fresh actual integer
+1792956319, captured 2026-10-25T19:25:19UTC. All other parsed values are identical.
+The exact control-plan04 and projection remain valid because registration is not
+in the projection. All plans/decisions remain qualification-pending, not qualified.
+
+`pending_plan_preflight(root,cfg)` uses the actual retained helper and frozen
+pending validator before bootstrap/parent Popen paths. The worker repeats the
+same real gate before observer.controls. Only the pinned private runner path is
+rebound, never the canonical historical runner; its path/cache/global mutations
+are restored in finally. Exact newly created private-engine module objects are
+removed through a scoped frozen-loader callback; existing selectors fail closed,
+and foreign replacements are preserved for boundary rejection. No future completed-control/eligible-plan input is added.
+This adds inventory/hash preflight time to the existing startup budget, no reset.
+
+Tests:
+- test_native_qualifier.py retains48 lifecycle/ownership/env tests. Their worker
+  engine-I/O fixture now also substitutes the schema gate, explicitly synthetic.
+- test_pending_plan_gate.py runs the actual source plan05 validator to full return
+  under a process-spawn deny sentinel; no successful runtime checks are mocked.
+  Negative mutated-plan reads are in-memory I/O seams, with real validator body.
+  Missing query file is simulated only through Path.is_file after runtime checks.
+  Actual bootstrap/parent bodies reject failed04 through the real schema gate
+  before Popen, with upstream request/review substituted only for that unit test.
+- fresh_pending_gate_probe.py creates the real88 graph in a fresh interpreter,
+  validates before and after baseline, and invokes frozen close unchanged. The
+  foreign mode inserts a fixture-owned nonstdlib module and requires rejection
+  with that exact registry object preserved. Neither mode replays contexts.
